---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { u } from "../consts";
---
<Base
  title="Our Story — How this started — Grimsley Mineral Co."
  description="It started because we kept buying rocks. How a shelf turned into a room, then into minerals, fossils, hand-built lava lamps and Taylor's nails, out of Grimsley, Tennessee."
  active=""
>
  <div class="pagehead">
    <div class="inner">
      <div class="crumb"><a href={u("")}>Home</a> / Our Story</div>
      <h1>Our Story</h1>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="prose">
    <p class="lead">This started because we kept buying rocks.</p>
    <p>Then a few more. Then a fossil, because it was sitting next to the rocks. Then a coin that somebody in the family had held onto. At some point the shelves stopped being shelves and became a room, and the room started needing a system.</p>
    <p>The lava lamps arrived sideways. We picked up old ones because they were cheap and strange, and then wanted to know how they worked, and then wanted to build one. Now the bases and caps get sculpted by hand and people commission them.</p>
    <p>Taylor paints nails. That has nothing to do with minerals and it is on this site anyway, because it comes out of the same room and the same hands. She takes a description like a color and a mood and turns it into a set that did not exist before.</p>
    <p>A lot of what we sell came from retired collectors breaking up cabinets they spent decades filling. Those pieces have a history longer than ours, and where we know it we pass it along: the locality, the collection it came out of, the condition, the parts we are unsure about. Where we do not know, we say we do not know. That is the whole promise, and it is the reason we would rather publish an unanswered question than a confident guess.</p>
    <p>We opened at the Highway 127 Yard Sale in August 2026. It is the largest yard sale in the country and it runs right down US-127, which is the road we are on. Everything runs online from here.</p>
    <p>We are still working out what this turns into. The <a href={u("journal")}>journal</a> is where that gets written down as it happens, including the parts that do not go well.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- The room does the rest of the telling. Nothing here asserts a date, an
       event or a locality, so nothing here needs confirming. -->
  <div class="photopair one">
    <figure>
      <img src={u("img/room/mineral-shelves-closeup-early.webp")} alt="Three white shelves packed with amethyst, quartz, geodes and mixed specimens" width="1600" height="2134" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <p style="margin-top:0;"><a class="btn btn-dark" href={u("journal")}>Read the journal</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>
